Fix the cut-off top of the worksheet instruction box

Paul, 2026-09-02: "the top of the instructions on this worksheet looks cut off."
He was right and it was my own rule that did it.

`.note` in worksheet.css carries only 12px of top padding, which is fine while
its first child brings its own margin. The previous commit added
`.note p { margin: 0 }` to tighten the list, which also zeroed the heading's
top margin - so "Before you start" sat hard against the top border while the
foot still had padding plus a divider under the closing line. Top-heavy, and it
reads as clipped.

Set the padding on the block instead of fighting margins, and target only the
first paragraph. 16px top, 14px bottom, and the closing line gets more room
above its divider.

⚠️ The rule worth keeping: never blanket-zero margins inside a shared
component. `.note` is used by every sheet type here, and a selector broad
enough to fix the spacing you are looking at is broad enough to break the
spacing you are not.
